ndance":18340,"officials":[{"fullName":"Kiel Murchison","displayName":"Kiel Murchison","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Garrett Rank","displayName":"Garrett Rank","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"James Tobias","displayName":"James Tobias","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Stephen Hiff","displayName":"Stephen Hiff","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Bruins beat Red Wings 4-1, spoil Detroit's Centennial celebration game","description":"— David Pastrnak had a goal and an assist as the Boston Bruins beat Detroit 4-1 on Wednesday night and spoiled the Red Wings' Centennial celebration game.","story":"DETROIT -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114778/david-pastrnak\">David Pastrnak</a> had a goal and an assist as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/bos/boston-bruins\">Boston Bruins</a> beat Detroit 4-1 on Wednesday night and spoiled the Red Wings' Centennial celebration game.\n\n\r\n              The contest was played on the 100th anniversary of Detroit’s first NHL game — a 2-0 loss for the then-Cougars to the Bruins. Pregame ceremonies on Wednesday included a video introduction from Scotty Bowman.\n\n\r\n              The centennial celebration resulted in a rare color-on-color game, with Detroit wearing red and the Bruins in black.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697438/jj-peterka\">JJ Peterka</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899949/pavel-zacha\">Pavel Zacha</a> also scored for the Bruins, who snapped a three-game skid. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697461/mason-lohrei\">Mason Lohrei</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4268466/morgan-geekie\">Morgan Geekie</a> each had two assists.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587994/daniil-tarasov\">Daniil Tarasov</a>, coming off a shutout of the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/tb/tampa-bay-lightning\">Tampa Bay Lightning</a>, made 27 saves, but couldn’t prevent Detroit’s sixth loss in seven games.\n\n\r\n              Detroit's <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697385/lucas-raymond\">Lucas Raymond</a> made it 1-0 at 16:58 of the first period. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3941546/keegan-kolesar\">Keegan Kolesar</a> knocked the puck loose in the neutral zone to set up a 2-on-1 break, and Raymond blasted Andrew Copp’s pass inside the left post for his ninth goal.\n\n\r\n              Peterka tied the game at 2:47 of the second, cutting in from the left wing and beating Tarasov on the glove side.\n\n\r\n              Zacha then gave the Bruins a 2-1 lead with a power-play goal at 11:48, putting in a rebound for his sixth of the season.\n\n\r\n              Pastrnak made it 3-1 at 5:11 of the third, beating Tarasov from the slot after a pass from Lohrei.\n\n\r\n              Casey Middelstadt finished the scoring into an empty net at 19:05.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Bruins: Host the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/wsh/washington-capitals\">Washington Capitals</a> on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Red Wings: Host the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyi/new-york-islanders\">New York Islanders</a> on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-19T03:26:34Z"}}